# speed08.env -- a speed setting for the ISPD 2008 standard, not part of it (HISTORY_COST_SWEEP.md Parts
# 140-141; the user's decision, 2026-10-20). Layer it last:
#   <name> bench/<design>.gr ./pd39route @standard.env @fast08.env @speed08.env
#
# The region stage's late searches flood their boxes (Part 138: 90-98% of the work from round 50 on), so
# its work is box area. Capping path A's region box at 100 (standard 200) cuts the residue runs 17-26%
# (newblue4 -26%, bigblue4 -20%, newblue7 -17%) and leaves 13 of the 16 designs identical; newblue1 28 vs 24
# and newblue4 144 vs 140 (both inside their run-to-run spread, but not gains), newblue3 / bigblue4 / newblue7
# unchanged. The reclaim path keeps 200: it starts from the overflow it injects (bigblue2: 20734) and needs
# wide boxes to clear it -- at 100 bigblue2 kept the longer path (+3.6% wirelength); at 200 its route is
# byte-identical to the standard's.
PD13ROUTE_REGION_BOX_CAP=100
PD39ROUTE_REGION_BOX_CAP_B=200
#
# The slow tier's plateau stop (Part 148, added 2026-10-23): stop once the best overflow has fallen less than
# 1% over the last 25 slow rounds while it is still >= 1000. Exact where the best had stopped moving (adaptec4
# hotspot 0.85: byte-identical, run -45%); where gains came after a flat stretch it costs a little -- newblue3
# +0.07% (run -15%), bigblue3 global 0.95 +0.56% (-14%). It never acts below 1000 (bigblue4, newblue7, and every
# design that converges).
PD39ROUTE_SLOW_PLATEAU=25,1,1000
#
# The batched region stage, gated (Parts 163-165b, added 2026-10-27): a region stage entering with at most 1000
# units of 2D overflow runs its rounds in batches of 64 nets (spread over 64 x 64 tiles) searched in parallel and
# committed in net order, with twice the round budget; above 1000 it is the sequential stage, unchanged.
# Portfolio variants running together share the machine's cores, recomputed every round. Measured with the
# standard + fast08: newblue3 byte-identical to the standard. With this whole file (Part 166): bigblue4 372 vs
# 360, 10008 s vs 29100 s before batching (the batched region rounds make no progress there); newblue7 102 vs
# 104, 18915 s vs 42800 s. Designs whose fallback never runs are untouched.
PD39ROUTE_REGION_BATCH=64,64
PD39ROUTE_REGION_BATCH_ROUNDS=2
PD39ROUTE_REGION_BATCH_MAX=1000
#
# The batched stage's sequential rerun (Part 167, added 2026-10-29): a batched region stage that ends having
# improved on its start by less than 1 unit puts its nets back on their entry routes and runs again as the
# sequential stage, exactly. bigblue4 (every variant's batched rounds stayed above the entering 406): 360,
# byte-identical to Part 141, in 22752 s (batched only: 372 in 10008 s). newblue7: no rerun, byte-identical
# to Part 166 (102, 18985 s).
PD39ROUTE_REGION_BATCH_FALLBACK=1
#
# The speculative portfolio (Part 168, added 2026-10-30; overrides fast08.env's `after`): the portfolio's variants
# start beside path A from its start state, path A keeping its full thread share, and are cancelled if it ends at
# or below the fallback threshold. Byte-identical to the gated portfolio on adaptec5, bigblue4, newblue1, newblue4
# and newblue7 (360 in 13095 s vs 22752 s; newblue1 2563 s vs 3503 s; newblue4 6748 s vs 7506 s). The price lands
# on designs that end at zero: the variants' copies are held from the start (adaptec5 peak memory 1660 -> 3137 MB,
# CPU +9%, wall time the same).
PD39ROUTE_PORTFOLIO_WHEN=speculative
#
# Refinement's stop below the plateau floor (Part 168, added 2026-10-30): below PD12ROUTE_PLATEAU_MIN, refinement
# stops after 20 iterations without gain. Refinement never raises overflow and restores its best, so the stop is
# exact while 20 exceeds every wait before a gain: in every variant of the four residues the longest was 7
# (newblue7), the last gain at iteration 12 or earlier, of 60. W=10 was run on newblue1 and newblue4, byte-identical
# (newblue1 1650 s, newblue4 5756 s with the speculative portfolio). Zero-overflow designs never refine above 0.
PD39ROUTE_REFINE_STOP=20
